#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:16
msgid "1. Why Per-Access Bounds Checks Hurt GPU Loops"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:18
msgid "Consider a naive matrix-multiply inner loop:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:20
msgid ""
"let mut sum = 0.0f32;\n"
"let mut i = 0;\n"
"while i < k {\n"
"    sum += a[row * k + i] * b[i * n + col];\n"
"    i += 1;\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:29
msgid "Each iteration executes three comparisons instead of one:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:31
msgid ""
"i < k               loop exit condition             (needed)\n"
"row * k + i < a.len bounds check + branch to trap   (overhead)\n"
"i * n + col < b.len bounds check + branch to trap   (overhead)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:37
msgid ""
"Those extra trap branches also split the loop body across basic blocks and "
"block loop unrolling. Because `a.len()` is an opaque runtime parameter to "
"`rustc`, the compiler cannot erase those checks unless you give it a strip "
"view, a launch precondition, or a `#[verify]` proof."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:41
msgid "2. Read Views: Check a Whole Row or Column Once"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:43
msgid ""
"A row-major matrix of width `stride` stores `(row, col)` at flat index `row "
"* stride + col`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:45
msgid ""
"3 x 4 matrix (stride = 4):\n"
"  row 0: [ 0   1   2   3 ]     row(1, 4) covers [4, 5, 6, 7]\n"
"  row 1: [ 4   5   6   7 ]     col(2, 3) covers [2, 6, 10] (step = 4)\n"
"  row 2: [ 8   9  10  11 ]\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:52
msgid ""
"`MatrixView32` wraps `&[f32]` with its row stride. Requesting `row(...)` or "
"`col(...)` performs **one** bounds check for the entire strip, and "
"`zip_exact` drives both strips with a single loop counter:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:54
msgid ""
"let a_mat = MatrixView32::new(a, k);\n"
"let b_mat = MatrixView32::new(b, n);\n"
"\n"
"if let Some(a_row) = a_mat.row(row, k)\n"
"    && let Some(b_col) = b_mat.col(col, k)\n"
"    && let Some(pair) = a_row.zip_exact(b_col)\n"
"{\n"
"    let mut sum = 0.0f32;\n"
"    for (x, y) in pair {\n"
"        sum += x * y;\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

