#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:77
msgid ""
"**Rule with `sync_threads()`**: Never return early before a block barrier if "
"a strip check fails. Use `.unwrap_or(RowView32::empty())` and "
"`.get(i).unwrap_or(0.0)` so out-of-range edge threads zero-fill and still "
"reach `thread::sync_threads()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:81
msgid "3. `requires`: Check Buffer Sizes Once on the Host"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:83
msgid ""
"`#[launch_contract(..., requires = (...))]` states buffer-length relations "
"right on the kernel:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:85
msgid ""
"#[kernel(launch_context = lc)]\n"
"#[launch_bounds(256)]\n"
"#[launch_contract(\n"
"    domain = 2,\n"
"    coordinates = u32,\n"
"    block = (16, 16, 1),\n"
"    requires = (k >= 1, a.len() >= m * k, b.len() >= k * n, c.len() >= m * "
"n),\n"
")]\n"
"pub fn sgemm_naive_views(\n"
"    m: u32, n: u32, k: u32, alpha: f32,\n"
"    a: &[f32], b: &[f32], beta: f32,\n"
"    mut c: DisjointSlice<f32, RuntimeRowMajorTiles<1, 1>>,\n"
") { ... }\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:101
msgid ""
"**Evaluated once on the CPU** inside `prepare_*` / typed launch using "
"checked `u64` arithmetic (so `m * k` cannot overflow and falsely pass)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:102
msgid ""
"**Clear host error** instead of a mid-kernel GPU trap when a buffer is "
"undersized:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:103
msgid ""
"sgemm_naive_views: size requirement `a.len() >= m * k` violated:\n"
"left-hand side is 8192, right-hand side is 16384\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:107
msgid ""
"**Feeds directly into `#[verify]`**: When paired with "
"`#[verify(no_oob_idx(...))]`, Lean 4 uses `requires` preconditions to prove "
"in-kernel indexing safe and erase `mir.assert` checks automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:111
msgid ""
"4. `#[verify(no_oob_idx(...))]` (preview): Erase General & Shared-Memory "
"Checks Safely"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:113
msgid ""
"Read views cover contiguous rows, columns, and fixed 2D tiles, while GPU "
"kernels also index `SharedArray` tiles (`TILE[ty * 16 + i]`), sub-warp bit-"
"splits (`S_X[tid * 4 + w]`), and multi-stage rings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:115
msgid ""
"Adding `#[verify(no_oob_idx(...))]` (preview) proves those index expressions "
"in Lean 4 at compile time and **deletes every proven `mir.assert` check "
"before PTX lowering** with zero `unsafe`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:117
msgid ""
"On 2D tiled SGEMM (`safe_gemm_views`), Lean 4 erases all 6 global and shared-"
"memory bounds checks (`~9,390 GFLOPS` on RTX 5090)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:118
msgid ""
"On 2-CTA Blackwell GEMM (`safe_gemm_sol_final`), Lean 4 erases all 27 shared-"
"memory and barrier-array checks (`2,118 TFLOPS` on B200, `100%+` of `--"
"unchecked-indexing`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:120
msgid ""
"See [Provably Safe Kernels (preview)](verified-kernels.md) for walkthroughs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:124
msgid "5. The Unverified Escape Hatch: `unchecked_indexing`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:126
msgid ""
"When you are prototyping an unverified kernel and accept full "
"`get_unchecked` responsibility, `#[kernel(unchecked_indexing)]` (or `--"
"unchecked-indexing` / `CUDA_OXIDE_UNCHECKED_INDEXING=1`) strips slice, "
"array, and `SharedArray` bounds checks without a proof:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:128
msgid ""
"#[kernel(unchecked_indexing)]\n"
"pub fn hot_loop(a: &[f32], b: &[f32], mut c: DisjointSlice<f32>) {\n"
"    let idx = thread::index_1d();\n"
"    let i = idx.get();\n"
"    if let Some(out) = c.get_mut(idx) {\n"
"        *out = a[i] + b[i]; // no check: OOB is undefined behavior\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:139
msgid ""
"**Narrow scope**: Removes only `x[i]` bounds checks inside that kernel; "
"division-by-zero, overflow, and range slicing (`&a[i..j]`) still trap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:140
msgid ""
"**Treat like `unsafe`**: Validate with `cargo oxide sanitize <target>` "
"(`compute-sanitizer --tool memcheck`) before enabling it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:144
msgid "Which Tool Should I Pick?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:146
msgid ""
"Need zero bounds-check overhead in a hot loop?\n"
"├── Row, column, or fixed 1D/2D tile?     -> MatrixView32 / LinearTiles + "
"`requires` (Safe, pure Rust)\n"
"├── SharedArray, bit-splits, or custom i? -> "
"`#[verify(no_oob_idx(...))]`            (Safe, proved in Lean 4)\n"
"└── Unverified prototype escape hatch?    -> "
"`#[kernel(unchecked_indexing)]`         (UB if out of bounds)\n"
msgstr ""
